        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T10:28:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there somewhere in the spec where this is called \"Credit\" ?\nIf not, I would prefer that we come up with another name because Credit is already used in L2CAP.\nAs the function is short and to enforce typing maybe two methods `SendCommandComplete` and `SendCommandStatus` here would make sense.\nAnd I think to match with the spec `num_command_credits_` \u003d\u003e `num_HCI_command_packets`",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9671f38_4fca7d53",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T16:22:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Host shall assume that sending of an HCI_Vendor_Specific_Debug\ncommand will consume an HCI command credit.\n\nI\u0027m not sure how many times, but it\u0027s definitely in the spec.  I agree that this could be more consistent, but I think the idea of a credit captures the meaning very nicely.  Since L2CAP is a different layer, I don\u0027t think there should be too much confusion.",
      "parentUuid": "ecb9a7d5_debb7d41",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a8ef832_7da6379f",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T16:37:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s in the spec then it\u0027s fine :+1:, I agree that credit is a good name for it.\n\nWhat do you think of limiting this function to only `CommandComplete` and `CommandStatus` ?",
      "parentUuid": "b9671f38_4fca7d53",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "929472e5_cae693f4",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T17:33:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good idea.  Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "2a8ef832_7da6379f",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e7ae4ca_f3b452a1",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T10:28:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we rewrite that to avoid the ternary here ?\nSomething like\n```\n// Some commands don\u0027t require credits.\nbool require_credits \u003d op \u003d\u003d OpCode::RESET || op \u003d\u003d OpCode::CONTROLLER_DEBUG_INFO;\nif (!(require_credits \u0026\u0026 num_command_credits_ \u003d\u003d 0)) {\n      ASSERT(num_command_credits_ \u003d\u003d 1);\n      num_command_credits_ -\u003d 1;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c8230b4_262ef6de",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T16:22:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the logic, maybe for the better, but it\u0027s not equivalent.\n\nHow about:\n    if (op !\u003d OpCode::RESET \u0026\u0026 op !\u003d OpCode::CONTROLLER_DEBUG_INFO) {\n      ASSERT(num_command_credits_ \u003d\u003d 1);\n      num_command_credits_ \u003d 0;\n    }",
      "parentUuid": "9e7ae4ca_f3b452a1",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9911e739_038f3746",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/model/controller/dual_mode_controller.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 434,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T16:37:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like how it looks, but I think this is missing the case were `num_command_credits_ \u003d\u003d 1` and `op \u003d\u003d OpCode::RESET || op \u003d\u003d OpCode::CONTROLLER_DEBUG_INFO`, in your current code it set the credits to 0 and there it keeps it to 1. I think the behaviour of setting it to 0 is what we want here ?",
      "parentUuid": "2c8230b4_262ef6de",
      "revId": "4fcc66fa729b9e6ce57efbc9372e281dd2397d2a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
